<title>GERMANY: German grain, beet crop conditions favourable - DWD.</title>
<headline>German grain, beet crop conditions favourable - DWD.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Showers in German grain areas have provided crops with enough moisture and warm temperatures are setting in, the DWD meteorological office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The weather is favourable for both winter and spring grains,&quot; a DWD source said.</p>
<p>Maize and beet crops were also developing according to plan and winter rapeseed continued to bloom.</p>
<p>DWD no longer expected night frosts, which damaged some winter grain last month. It noted warm temperatures and rain increase the risk of fungi.</p>
<p>Maximum day temperatures up to May 21 were forecast between 17 and 25 degrees compared with 13 to 25 degrees in the seven day period up to May 14.</p>
<p>Farmers were beginning to cut grass for silage which could help reduce the demand for bought-in feeds in the summer season. -Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
